      "accepted_text": "TRADEMOOT FEATURES\nOld Town Glassworks. Old gnome artificer forges, a glass-\ncapped astronomical observatory, crystalline statues, glass\nfountains, ornate windows.\nRuined Rune Teleportation Circle. In the basement of the\nRuined Rune Inn is a permanent 'destination' Teleportation\nCircle dating back to the Ruined Rune dwarves. See\ndescription in the Magic Items section.\nShrines. There are no temples in Trademoot, but that absence is\nsupplanted by a scattering of shrines, as follows:\n• Dumathoin: an old copper statue of a male dwarf miner\n• Nebelun (Gond): a tempered-glass statue of a male gnome\nartisan\n• Waukeen: an ornate statue of a female woman merchant\nWaukeen's Daffodils. Waukeen, the deity of commerce, has the\nlargest following in Trademoot. She has taken notice of\nTrademoot, occasionally blessing it with Daffodils. The first\ncreature to discover a new Daffodil sprouting and leave a gold\ncoin beside it will receive a point of inspiration each of the next\ntwo mornings."
